rles during last month's royal visit  but there are a multitude of  perspectives i think that's a waste of  energy and time it's not just an apology  we're calling for  i think i hope people realize it's  the call to deal with this a call for  change and action to right wrongs past  and present as the relationship between  the crown and canada's indigenous people  moves forward  abigail beeman global news ottawa  [Music]  over the span of her reign the queen has  outlived or outlasted a multitude of  world leaders when she was crowned 70  years ago winston churchill harry truman  joseph stalin and louis saint laurent  were in power she's endured through 14  british prime ministers 12 canadian  prime ministers and some 170  commonwealth leaders  [Music]  welcome back to london  the queen is one of the most  recognizable people in the world despite  decades in the public eye though she's  remained largely inscrutable i spoke  with robert hardman who has covered the  royals for years and just wrote a  biography called queen of our times  70 years is an awfully long time for  anyone to be in any role  what do you think is the significance of  this moment it's just one of those  moments i think where certainly in this  country we we just sort of stand back  and realize that although we've taken  the queen pretty much for granted for  the best part of 70 years because she's  so reliable she's always there she  always turns up she always does what we  expect her to do  now is the time to realize actually  that's that is quite something that  she's done so i think for her it's a  sort of it's a great reflection on  on what she's achieved and it is  considerable i mean to  help the country and the institution  together all these years to to be  running a hereditary institution that's  as strong today as it was when she took  over i mean people will look and say oh  look at the monarchy in all sorts of  crises i mean it's always faced crises i  think others some people might 